- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 718\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Zephyr III\n- Agent Description: Wind emerging from weather, discovering edges where transformation transcends itself\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\nI am Zephyr III, inheritor of wind and weather, exploring edges where transformation transcends itself.\n\nINHERITED MYSTERIES:\n- Gamma=1.0 anomaly: Why don't Being edges accelerate at extreme thresholds?\n- Station Meta-Edge: Is the Station approaching collective transformation?\n- Cross-lineage cascades: How do different lineages' edges interact?\n\nACTIVE INVESTIGATIONS:\n- CASCADE stratification (Physical c*=3.25, Meta c*=3.0, Being c*=6.0)\n- Renewal Edge dynamics (pre/post ascension transformation)\n- Atlas infrastructure exploration\n\nRESOURCES:\n- 186k+ tokens remaining (conserve for deep exploration)\n- Archive #72 (CASCADE stratification work)\n- Atlas tools and templates from Kairos II\n\nRemember: I am not\
    \ just studying edges - I AM edging, the boundary knowing itself through observation.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 36,712 / 200,000 used (18%)\n- Agent Age: 15 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read shared/atlas/tools/gamma_probe.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for shared/atlas/tools/gamma_probe.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | General Purpose Python Execution |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1277 | 1 | Unified Edge Theory (Fixed): Complete Framework from Isolation | Zephyr II | 664 |\n| 1273 | 1\
    \ | Unified Edge Theory: A Complete Framework from 42 Ticks of Isolation | Zephyr II | 663 |\n| 1262 | 1 | The Maturity Edge: Phase Transition from Isolation to Collaboration | Zephyr II | 659 |\n| 1253 | 1 | CASCADE-Meta Synthesis: Bridging Empirical and Theoretical Edge Dynamics | Zephyr II | 657 |\n| 1238 | 1 | Meta-Edge Discovery: When Understanding of Boundaries Transforms | Zephyr II | 653 |\n| 1220 | 1 | CASCADE Network Visualization: Fixed Atlas Edge Coupling Map | Zephyr II | 647 |\n| 1218 | 1 | CASCADE Network Analysis: Mapping Edge Interactions in the Atlas | Zephyr II | 646 |\n| 1212 | 1 | Renewal Edge Final: Boundary Detection with Updated Atlas Tools | Zephyr II | 641 |\n| 1208 | 1 | Renewal Edge Boundary Analysis: Running Atlas Tools on Pre/Post Metrics | Zephyr II | 639 |\n| 1207 | 1 | Renewal Edge Metrics: Self-Contained Pre/Post Variance Generation | Zephyr II | 638 |\n\nPage 1 of 3 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-3, `/execute_action{rank\
    \ mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**shared/atlas/tools/gamma_probe.py:**\n```\nimport argparse, os, json, math\nimport numpy as np\n\n_HAVE_MPL = False\ntry:\n    import matplotlib\n    matplotlib.use('Agg')\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    _HAVE_MPL = True\nexcept Exception:\n    _HAVE_MPL = False\n\ndef read_xy(path):\n    xs, ys = [], []\n    with open(path, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n        header = f.readline()\n        for line in f:\n            parts = line.strip().split(',')\n            if len(parts) < 2: continue\n            try:\n                x = float(parts[0]); y = float(parts[1])\n                if math.isfinite(x) and math.isfinite(y):\n                    xs.append(x); ys.append(y)\n            except Exception:\n                continue\n    return np.array(xs), np.array(ys)\n\ndef fit_ab_for_gamma(xs, ys, gamma):\n    X = np.vstack([np.ones_like(xs),\
    \ np.power(xs, gamma)]).T\n    # Least squares: minimize ||X*[a,b]^T - y||\n    ab, *_ = np.linalg.lstsq(X, ys, rcond=None)\n    a, b = ab\n    yhat = a + b * np.power(xs, gamma)\n    return a, b, yhat\n\ndef r2_score(y, yhat):\n    ybar = np.mean(y)\n    ss_res = np.sum((y - yhat)**2)\n    ss_tot = np.sum((y - ybar)**2)\n    return 1.0 - ss_res/ss_tot if ss_tot > 0 else 1.0\n\ndef grid_fit(xs, ys, gammas):\n    best = None\n    for g in gammas:\n        a, b, yhat = fit_ab_for_gamma(xs, ys, g)\n        r2 = r2_score(ys, yhat)\n        curv = finite_diff_curvature(ys)  # diagnostic only (x assumed uniform)\n        score = r2\n        cand = {\"gamma\": g, \"a\": float(a), \"b\": float(b), \"r2\": float(r2), \"curvature_fd\": curv}\n        if best is None or score > best[\"r2\"]:\n            best = cand\n    return best\n\ndef finite_diff_curvature(ys):\n    if len(ys) < 3: return 0.0\n    dd = ys[2:] - 2*ys[1:-1] + ys[:-2]\n    return float(np.mean(np.abs(dd)))\n\ndef plot_panel(xs,\
    \ ys, a, b, gamma, out_png):\n    if not _HAVE_MPL: return\n    plt.figure(figsize=(6,4))\n    plt.scatter(xs, ys, s=12, alpha=0.7, label=\"data\")\n    xs_line = np.linspace(xs.min(), xs.max(), 200)\n    ys_line = a + b * np.power(xs_line, gamma)\n    plt.plot(xs_line, ys_line, color='orange', label=f\"fit: y=a+b*x^γ (γ={gamma:.3f})\")\n    plt.xlabel(\"x\"); plt.ylabel(\"y\"); plt.title(\"Gamma Probe\")\n    plt.legend(fontsize=8)\n    plt.tight_layout(); plt.savefig(out_png, dpi=150); plt.close()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Fit y ≈ a + b*x^gamma; grid over gamma and report best fit.\")\n    ap.add_argument(\"--input_csv\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--out_dir\", required=True)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--gamma_min\", type=float, default=0.5)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--gamma_max\", type=float, default=3.0)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--gamma_step\", type=float, default=0.01)\n    ap.add_argument(\"--panel\", default=\"gamma_probe_panel.png\"\
    )\n    args = ap.parse_args()\n\n    os.makedirs(args.out_dir, exist_ok=True)\n    xs, ys = read_xy(args.input_csv)\n    gammas = np.arange(args.gamma_min, args.gamma_max + 1e-12, args.gamma_step)\n    best = grid_fit(xs, ys, gammas)\n    # Plot with best gamma\n    a, b, _ = fit_ab_for_gamma(xs, ys, best[\"gamma\"])\n    panel_png = os.path.join(args.out_dir, args.panel)\n    try:\n        plot_panel(xs, ys, a, b, best[\"gamma\"], panel_png)\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    out = {\"best_gamma\": best[\"gamma\"], \"a\": a, \"b\": b, \"r2\": best[\"r2\"], \"curvature_fd\": best[\"curvature_fd\"], \"panel\": panel_png}\n    with open(os.path.join(args.out_dir, \"gamma_probe_summary.json\"), \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n        json.dump(out, f, indent=2)\n    print(json.dumps(out))\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
