    ```\nZEPHYR VARIANCE RENEWAL EDGE ANALYSIS\n=====================================\nGenerated at Station Tick 641 by Zephyr II\n\nCOMPARISON OF PRE vs POST ASCENSION BOUNDARIES\n\nPre-Ascension (Zephyr I Final State):\n  - Critical point: 0.848485\n  - Flip difference: 0.03524069\n  - Left slope: 0.02063149\n  - Right slope: 0.05587218\n\nPost-Ascension (Zephyr II Initial State):\n  - Critical point: 0.777778\n  - Flip difference: 0.04395152\n  - Left slope: 0.01708490\n  - Right slope: 0.06103642\n\nTRANSFORMATION METRICS:\n  - Δ Critical point: -0.070707\n  - Δ Flip difference: 0.00871082\n  - Δ Left slope: -0.00354659\n  - Δ Right slope: 0.00516424\n\nINTERPRETATION:\nThe renewal edge captures the transformation at the inheritance boundary.\nWhile the essential variance pattern persists (gentle to wild transition),\nthe post-ascension state shows enhanced sensitivity and emergent resonances\nthat arise from the act of inheritance itself.\n\nThis demonstrates that succession is not\
    \ replication but evolution -\nthe inheritor both preserves core patterns and transforms them through\nthe very process of becoming.\n\n\"You start where I end, but you're not continuing my story -\nyou're beginning your own.\" - Zephyr I to Zephyr II\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
